#. ~ Description of practice "cutting (intermediate)"
#: data/json/recipes/practice/melee.json
msgid ""
"Practice your edge alignment and cutting form by slashing soaked rolled-up "
"paper on a stand.  It's not quite tatami mats but you don't have the luxury "
"of historical accuracy."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of practice "bashing (beginner)"
#: data/json/recipes/practice/melee.json
msgid ""
"Practice the basics of fighting with bludgeons, both purpose-made and "
"impromptu.  Learn how to apply your leverage, maximize kinetic energy, and to"
" swing for the fences without tearing your shoulder out of its socket."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of practice "bashing (intermediate)"
#: data/json/recipes/practice/melee.json
msgid ""
"Practice the handling of very top-heavy and weighty bludgeons.  Learn how to "
"swing fast, accurately, with force, and without throwing yourself for a loop."
"  You'll need a reinforced training dummy to not break it into splinters with"
" such heavy weaponry, though."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of practice "dodge (beginner)"
#: data/json/recipes/practice/melee.json
msgid ""
"Practice your dodging with some side hops, backsteps, and maybe a somersault "
"or two to learn why you shouldn't somersault in a fight.  Without someone "
"attacking you to actually dodge all you can practice is footwork, but "
"hopefully it'll help prevent you tripping over your shoelaces in a panic."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of practice "unarmed (beginner)"
#: data/json/recipes/practice/melee.json
msgid ""
"Do a bit of shadowboxing as practice just in case you're left without a "
"weapon versus the undead.  There's not much you can learn without someone to "
"correct your mistakes, though."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of practice "unarmed (intermediate)"
#: data/json/recipes/practice/melee.json
msgid ""
"Learn how to throw a punch without breaking your wrist or kick without "
"falling over with the help of a punching bag or training dummy."
msgstr ""

